  "description": "GUBGET crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H69 B6 N36 O9 Sm5. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 2 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm5 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm6 (Sm) has 2 O neighbors; Sm7 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm8 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm9 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm10 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.625-4.904 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.20-168.56°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C54H69B6N36O9Sm5. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
